WEBVTT

01:35.970 --> 01:37.430
<i>Am I just dancing like a puppet</i>

01:37.430 --> 01:39.516
<i>on Kisaki's string again?</i>

01:40.308 --> 01:41.392
<i>And...</i>

01:41.976 --> 01:44.437
Beware of a traitor.

01:45.105 --> 01:47.023
<i>Does that mean one of these guys</i>

01:47.023 --> 01:49.192
<i>has connections with Kisaki?</i>

01:49.818 --> 01:51.277
What's wrong, Takemitchy?

01:51.277 --> 01:53.196
Uh... Oh, nothing.

01:59.077 --> 02:03.248
This emergency meeting
of the Tokyo Manji Gang will now begin!

02:04.874 --> 02:07.335
You and I are enemies.

02:07.335 --> 02:08.628
<i>Oh, right.</i>

02:09.212 --> 02:13.633
<i>Kaku-chan may have said that
to throw us into confusion.</i>

02:14.259 --> 02:17.387
<i>Until I can be sure, I'd better not...</i>

02:18.388 --> 02:22.475
Yesterday, members of our gang
were attacked all over Tokyo.

02:22.475 --> 02:25.145
It was the work of Tenjiku,
a gang from Yokohama.

02:25.687 --> 02:27.147
Tenjiku? You know it?

02:27.147 --> 02:28.481
Never heard of it.

02:28.481 --> 02:31.651
Tenjiku is a recently-formed gang.

02:31.651 --> 02:33.695
We don't know
what kind of gang they are yet.

02:34.279 --> 02:35.905
The first to be attacked was

02:35.905 --> 02:38.366
First Division. Step forward!

02:40.910 --> 02:45.081
The ones who attacked us
called themselves Team Mochizuki.

02:45.081 --> 02:46.666
Team Mochizuki?

02:46.666 --> 02:51.462
That's the team run by Kanji Mochizuki,
the ex-leader of Jugem.

02:51.963 --> 02:54.299
They're probably Tenjiku's main force.

02:54.299 --> 02:56.885
Mochizuki? You mean that Mocchi?

02:56.885 --> 03:00.805
Mocchi of Jugem?
He's one of the S-62 Generation.

03:02.140 --> 03:03.766
<i>S-62 Generation?</i>

03:04.893 --> 03:07.604
Their main force isn't just Mocchi.

03:07.604 --> 03:08.688
Huh?

03:09.397 --> 03:12.775
The Haitani Brothers
are also part of Tenjiku.

03:12.775 --> 03:15.403
The Haitanis who control Roppongi?

03:15.403 --> 03:17.780
They're all members
of the S-62 Generation.

03:17.780 --> 03:18.865
Huh?

03:19.532 --> 03:24.329
Mikey, the other guys who got beat up
all said the same thing.

03:24.329 --> 03:25.997
That Madarame got them.

03:27.290 --> 03:31.711
The ghost of the ninth generation
BLACK DRAGON that we crushed.

03:31.711 --> 03:35.548
Madarame's also part
of the S-62 Generation.

03:35.548 --> 03:36.758
What?

03:37.342 --> 03:39.385
In other words, Tenjiku is a gang

03:39.385 --> 03:44.307
made up of the S-62 Generation guys,
who normally wouldn't have teamed up.

03:44.807 --> 03:47.560
Sounds like
their grudge against Toman runs deep.

03:49.938 --> 03:51.147
In any case,

03:51.648 --> 03:53.900
I won't let us keep getting beat!

03:53.900 --> 03:56.194
We're going to invade Yokohama next!

03:56.194 --> 03:57.320
What?

03:57.904 --> 03:59.530
Damn right!

03:59.530 --> 04:00.615
For sure!

04:00.615 --> 04:02.408
Those damn upstarts!

04:02.408 --> 04:04.911
The S-62 Generation
is a bunch of old fossils.

04:05.578 --> 04:07.038
- Oh, no...
- Huh?

04:07.705 --> 04:10.833
I'm going to build my own Toman.

04:11.918 --> 04:13.336
I get the feeling...

04:13.795 --> 04:16.547
that this fight is going
exactly the way Kisaki wants it to.

04:16.547 --> 04:19.634
- But there's no stopping it now.
- Huh?

04:19.634 --> 04:22.512
Oh, yeah. I guess you're right.

04:23.054 --> 04:24.097
But...

04:24.097 --> 04:26.432
Then confirm your feelings.

04:26.641 --> 04:28.726
Huh? What do you mean?

04:28.726 --> 04:30.728
You really are an idiot.

04:30.728 --> 04:32.939
I'm asking what you mean!

04:32.939 --> 04:35.692
You're able to know
what happens in the future.

04:35.692 --> 04:37.944
I know you vowed not to go back,

04:37.944 --> 04:40.029
but what's wrong with going back
when you need to?

04:40.363 --> 04:41.406
Oh...

04:41.406 --> 04:42.865
Time for all of Toman

04:42.865 --> 04:44.909
to fight Tenjiku!

04:47.870 --> 04:49.831
Go talk with Naoto in the future.

04:49.831 --> 04:51.541
You should find some information.

04:52.041 --> 04:53.042
Okay.

04:57.130 --> 04:59.590
<i>I want to know all I can
about the situation</i>

04:59.590 --> 05:00.758
<i>and how things turn out.</i>

05:01.217 --> 05:04.512
<i>What's happening right now?
And what will happen next?</i>

05:04.971 --> 05:07.140
<i>What is Kisaki up to?</i>

05:08.308 --> 05:09.767
<i>And can he...</i>

05:10.184 --> 05:12.854
<i>can Tetta Kisaki really
travel through time?</i>

05:13.313 --> 05:16.566
<i>I didn't want to return
to that crappy future.</i>

05:16.566 --> 05:17.692
<i>But I've got no choice!</i>

05:25.033 --> 05:28.828
<i>I'll go back as often as it takes
to change the future.</i>

05:30.330 --> 05:32.081
Takemichi?

05:33.583 --> 05:34.667
Hina?

05:38.087 --> 05:39.088
What the...

05:40.715 --> 05:42.091
Have you been fighting again?

05:42.759 --> 05:45.511
<i>Yeah, just like I vowed that day,</i>

05:45.511 --> 05:48.097
<i>before the rising flames.</i>

05:48.723 --> 05:51.559
I just keep on losing.

05:51.559 --> 05:52.643
Oh, you!

05:52.643 --> 05:55.563
<i>I'll keep on trying,
over and over again.</i>

06:02.487 --> 06:05.448
<i>I told Naoto
every new thing I learned in the past</i>

06:05.948 --> 06:07.742
<i>and everything I had thought over.</i>

06:08.326 --> 06:09.369
I see.

06:09.911 --> 06:12.372
If Kisaki really can travel through time,

06:13.289 --> 06:14.707
then we must kill him.

06:15.833 --> 06:17.835
Huh? Hold on, Naoto.

06:17.835 --> 06:22.256
It's pointless if he keeps tampering
every time you change the past.

06:22.715 --> 06:24.467
Killing him in the past is the only way.

06:24.467 --> 06:25.802
You can't be serious.

06:25.802 --> 06:27.220
I'm kidding.

06:27.929 --> 06:30.515
But if it's true,
you're just playing cat and mouse.

06:31.265 --> 06:34.644
To him, what you're doing
is tampering with things.

06:34.644 --> 06:36.813
Well, that's true, but...

06:36.813 --> 06:39.649
Killing you in the past
would be the easiest thing to do.

06:39.649 --> 06:41.567
Hey, whose side are you on?

06:42.944 --> 06:46.030
I wonder
what Kisaki's current goal in the past is.

06:46.030 --> 06:47.156
Huh?

06:48.574 --> 06:53.121
Kisaki 12 years ago is using Tenjiku
to take over Toman.

06:53.955 --> 06:55.039
But in the present,

06:55.039 --> 06:57.875
the police don't even know
the name Tenjiku.

06:58.459 --> 07:00.086
And Kisaki is dead.

07:00.086 --> 07:03.965
So that means... Kisaki failed.

07:04.674 --> 07:07.218
<i>Did something happen
that Kisaki didn't foresee?</i>

07:08.136 --> 07:09.220
Huh?

07:10.012 --> 07:11.514
"Izana Kurokawa"?

07:12.014 --> 07:17.103
My hero now is the leader of Tenjiku,
Izana Kurokawa.

07:17.562 --> 07:19.689
Whoa! Naoto!

07:19.689 --> 07:21.941
Who's that Izana Kurokawa guy?

07:21.941 --> 07:23.025
Him?

07:23.651 --> 07:25.445
One of Toman's top brass.

07:25.445 --> 07:28.781
I think he used to be
the leader of BLACK DRAGON.

07:28.781 --> 07:29.866
What?

07:30.450 --> 07:32.160
The leader of BLACK DRAGON?

07:32.702 --> 07:34.704
That's crazy, Naoto.

07:34.704 --> 07:37.707
He's Tenjiku's leader.

07:38.541 --> 07:39.667
What's going on?

07:40.209 --> 07:42.211
It's not like what I saw in the past.

07:42.795 --> 07:44.088
He's Tenjiku's leader?

07:44.589 --> 07:46.174
But that gang didn't even...

07:46.174 --> 07:48.426
Yes, it does exist,
in the past.

07:48.426 --> 07:52.555
It's a gang created by guys
from something called the S-62 Generation.

07:52.555 --> 07:54.098
Kisaki's among them.

07:54.557 --> 07:56.726
And he's their leader, huh?

07:56.726 --> 07:57.810
Yeah.

07:58.936 --> 08:02.190
If you've seen this guy, Izana Kurokawa,

08:02.773 --> 08:05.151
then it's probably worth looking into him.

08:05.943 --> 08:08.488
I'll check him out
on the police information net.

08:08.946 --> 08:09.989
And Tenjiku too.

08:10.573 --> 08:12.116
Do it as fast as you can.

08:12.658 --> 08:15.203
Until then,
I'll do some digging on my own.

08:15.870 --> 08:17.497
- Takemichi.
- Huh?

08:18.664 --> 08:21.584
I hope we can end it this time.

08:22.460 --> 08:25.463
Yeah. Let's end it, Naoto.

08:25.963 --> 08:26.964
Right.

08:29.509 --> 08:32.303
<i>I said I'd do some digging,</i>

08:32.720 --> 08:35.056
<i>but I've got no idea where to look.</i>

08:36.390 --> 08:38.017
BLACK DRAGON, huh?

08:38.768 --> 08:40.019
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

08:40.019 --> 08:43.856
<i>I wonder what those former BLACK DRAGON
members Inupi and Koko are doing now.</i>

08:44.524 --> 08:47.276
<i>They weren't on Naoto's list of the dead.</i>

08:47.944 --> 08:51.155
<i>I might learn something
if I can meet up with them.</i>

08:52.156 --> 08:54.951
But I've got no idea where they might be.

08:55.243 --> 08:56.994
Huh? Oh.

09:08.381 --> 09:10.341
I'm going to defeat you

09:11.092 --> 09:12.718
and take over BLACK DRAGON.

09:15.930 --> 09:17.974
<i>It's been 12 years since then.</i>

09:18.432 --> 09:20.810
<i>But it feels like yesterday to me.</i>

09:22.728 --> 09:24.355
<i>After that fight,</i>

09:24.355 --> 09:28.317
<i>I figured it would change things
for the better in the future.</i>

09:29.193 --> 09:31.529
<i>I stopped Yuzuha from killing Taiju,</i>

09:31.529 --> 09:34.115
<i>and BLACK DRAGON
fell under First Division's command.</i>

09:34.699 --> 09:36.576
<i>I also managed
to kick Kisaki out of Toman.</i>

09:37.285 --> 09:40.997
<i>But the future didn't get one bit better.</i>

09:40.997 --> 09:42.915
<i>In fact, it's gotten worse.</i>

09:44.125 --> 09:45.960
Aw, damn it!

09:45.960 --> 09:48.296
What the hell am I supposed to do?

09:49.922 --> 09:51.132
Oops.

09:51.132 --> 09:52.341
Keep it down.

09:52.675 --> 09:53.926
Oh, sorry.

09:54.552 --> 09:58.222
Pray that he may rest in peace too.

09:58.639 --> 09:59.640
I will.

10:00.600 --> 10:02.685
Huh? "He"?

10:03.185 --> 10:05.354
Since he died,

10:05.354 --> 10:08.149
I've been coming here every day.

10:09.275 --> 10:10.276
Huh?

10:10.818 --> 10:15.072
I wonder
if Hakkai's still a weakling in heaven.

10:16.907 --> 10:17.908
Amen.

10:18.576 --> 10:19.827
Taiju?

10:30.254 --> 10:31.672
<i>The leader of</i>

10:32.173 --> 10:34.508
<i>the 10th generation BLACK DRAGON...</i>

10:36.135 --> 10:37.511
<i>Taiju Shiba.</i>

10:38.429 --> 10:40.640
They've all died.

10:41.223 --> 10:44.310
How've you been, Hanagaki?

10:45.353 --> 10:48.856
<i>I've found a survivor
who knows about Toman's past.</i>

10:49.440 --> 10:50.566
It's been a while.

10:50.858 --> 10:52.818
Could I talk with you for a bit?

10:52.818 --> 10:54.028
Huh?

10:54.612 --> 10:57.073
There are some things I've got to know

10:57.657 --> 10:59.325
about Izana Kurokawa and BLACK DRAGON.

11:03.996 --> 11:05.122
Uh...

11:05.122 --> 11:07.124
This is Naoto Tachibana,

11:07.124 --> 11:09.669
an old neighborhood friend
who works for the police now.

11:09.669 --> 11:11.212
Nice to meet you.

11:11.212 --> 11:12.421
And this is...

11:12.421 --> 11:13.714
- Hmm.
- Uh...

11:14.298 --> 11:16.676
Enough with introductions. Come with me.

11:20.179 --> 11:23.265
Listen. I've got no intention
of cooperating with the cops.

11:23.724 --> 11:25.559
But because of Hakkai,

11:25.559 --> 11:28.396
I've got a grudge against Toman.

11:28.396 --> 11:29.772
We'll trade intel.

11:30.564 --> 11:31.565
All right.

11:31.899 --> 11:34.985
Order anything you like. This is my place.

11:34.985 --> 11:36.821
Whoa! You're the owner?

11:37.321 --> 11:39.407
So, what you want to know is

11:39.407 --> 11:43.327
about Izana Kurokawa
and BLACK DRAGON, right?

11:43.327 --> 11:48.666
Right. Izana Kurokawa was the leader
of the gang Tenjiku, so why...

11:49.250 --> 11:51.627
Taiju, do you know of Tenjiku?

11:52.086 --> 11:55.089
They used to be a gang in Yokohama.

11:55.089 --> 11:58.217
So they did exist, didn't they?

11:58.217 --> 11:59.301
Huh?

12:00.678 --> 12:04.515
There wasn't much, but there were reports
with the Kanagawa Police.

12:04.515 --> 12:06.642
How did this Izana Kurokawa guy

12:06.642 --> 12:10.980
become the leader of BLACK DRAGON
and become part of Toman now?

12:10.980 --> 12:12.690
That's not quite right.

12:13.149 --> 12:14.150
Huh?

12:14.859 --> 12:16.652
You've got the order wrong.

12:20.531 --> 12:25.286
Do you know who actually founded
BLACK DRAGON in the first place?

12:25.870 --> 12:26.954
Who founded it?

12:28.414 --> 12:32.710
The first generation BLACK DRAGON leader
was Shinichiro Sano.

12:32.710 --> 12:35.004
What?

12:35.004 --> 12:39.341
The guy who founded BLACK DRAGON
was Mikey's older brother.

12:40.509 --> 12:43.387
<i>When he led the tough dudes of Tokyo,</i>

12:43.387 --> 12:45.556
<i>he was always a brilliant sight.</i>

12:46.932 --> 12:51.812
Mikey's big brother
was the founder of BLACK DRAGON?

12:52.396 --> 12:53.481
That's right.

12:53.481 --> 12:56.108
The original BLACK DRAGON was legendary.

12:56.609 --> 13:01.197
That was carried on by the second
and third generations and beyond.

13:03.991 --> 13:09.163
Then the eighth generation leader,
Izana Kurokawa, took command.

13:09.163 --> 13:10.581
Eighth generation?

13:10.581 --> 13:13.000
You mean he was before you?

13:13.000 --> 13:14.502
Yeah.

13:14.502 --> 13:17.671
<i>When Toman was formed,
they crushed the ninth generation.</i>

13:17.671 --> 13:20.674
<i>That means the eighth generation
was before Toman was formed.</i>

13:21.383 --> 13:24.762
So Izana Kurokawa is older than you?

13:24.762 --> 13:28.224
He's two years older,
in the S-62 Generation.

13:28.224 --> 13:30.559
S-62 Generation?

13:30.559 --> 13:32.102
Those are Tenjiku guys!

13:32.603 --> 13:34.021
<i>There's the connection!</i>

13:34.522 --> 13:38.776
Three years after Izana Kurokawa
left BLACK DRAGON,

13:38.776 --> 13:42.363
he formed Yokohama's Tenjiku
and fought with Toman.

13:42.863 --> 13:45.741
That was the Kanto Incident.

13:46.283 --> 13:48.828
Let the Kanto Incident begin.

13:49.328 --> 13:51.831
<i>That's what's happening now 12 years ago.</i>

13:52.373 --> 13:53.791
Who won?

13:53.791 --> 13:54.875
Takemichi.

13:54.875 --> 13:55.960
Huh? Oh...

13:55.960 --> 13:58.504
Huh? You should know.

13:58.504 --> 14:00.047
Uh, well...

14:00.047 --> 14:04.885
Since you were in Toman, it figures
you don't want to acknowledge it.

14:06.971 --> 14:10.349
It was a drawn-out fight
that ended in an unexpected deal.

14:11.559 --> 14:13.352
<i>So neither side won.</i>

14:13.853 --> 14:15.938
<i>At the top was Manjiro Sano.</i>

14:16.313 --> 14:18.482
<i>Second in command was Tetta Kisaki.</i>

14:18.858 --> 14:21.235
<i>Third in command was Izana Kurokawa.</i>

14:22.403 --> 14:24.738
Toman and Tenjiku combined into one

14:24.738 --> 14:27.700
to create the vilest gang in history.

14:28.200 --> 14:31.161
<i>Kisaki... It's the same again.</i>

14:31.161 --> 14:33.038
<i>He still ends up in Toman!</i>

14:34.039 --> 14:37.918
Huh? Wait, but Kisaki's dead.

14:38.669 --> 14:41.130
- Did he really die?
- Huh?

14:41.130 --> 14:44.842
Is Kisaki actually dead?

14:44.842 --> 14:46.677
Naoto Tachibana.

14:46.677 --> 14:47.887
Huh?

14:47.887 --> 14:48.971
Takemichi.

14:49.471 --> 14:51.682
I looked into Izana Kurokawa again.

14:52.641 --> 14:55.019
He's got a lot of influence
over the police.

14:55.019 --> 14:56.186
What?

14:56.186 --> 14:58.814
I found evidence
that records had been revised.

14:59.398 --> 15:02.276
Kurokawa is much bigger than we thought.

15:02.276 --> 15:03.444
You mean...

15:04.069 --> 15:06.322
He made it look like Kisaki is dead.

15:06.322 --> 15:08.032
Isn't that right?

15:09.199 --> 15:12.620
He let Kisaki escape abroad,
as Kisaki was a suspect in various crimes.

15:13.162 --> 15:15.247
A corpse was prepared to fake his death.

15:15.247 --> 15:17.499
You're kidding.
Then Kisaki is...

15:18.834 --> 15:19.960
He's alive.

15:21.378 --> 15:23.422
My research before was insufficient.

15:25.299 --> 15:27.259
Sano's dead.

15:28.052 --> 15:29.803
And Kisaki's gone abroad.

15:30.304 --> 15:34.433
So in reality,
the leader of Toman now is Izana Kurokawa.

15:34.433 --> 15:37.269
This jerk's the leader of Toman?

15:37.269 --> 15:39.605
Why? Why is this bastard the leader?

15:40.105 --> 15:41.941
I don't know why.

15:42.483 --> 15:45.110
But I do know that Manjiro Sano had

15:45.110 --> 15:48.906
even greater trust in Izana Kurokawa
than in Ken Ryuguji.

15:48.906 --> 15:50.783
More than Draken?

15:51.533 --> 15:54.411
<i>Who the hell is this Izana Kurokawa?</i>

15:55.412 --> 15:57.164
Well, well.

15:57.748 --> 16:01.752
Two of my former bosses
are having a private meeting, huh?

16:03.629 --> 16:04.797
Very suspicious.

16:05.297 --> 16:07.549
<i>Huh? Koko and Inupi?</i>

16:07.549 --> 16:09.301
You bastards.

16:09.301 --> 16:12.888
What the hell do you think you're doing
bringing Toman goons in here?

16:12.888 --> 16:16.392
We're here to abduct you
on Kurokawa's orders.

16:16.392 --> 16:20.980
We heard there was a rat from the cops
snooping around.

16:21.188 --> 16:25.109
So I tailed him, and I found
two of my former bosses as well.

16:26.151 --> 16:28.988
Since you've been snooping
for information about Izana Kurokawa,

16:28.988 --> 16:31.156
you've been designated as Toman enemies.

16:33.993 --> 16:37.204
You idiots think you can stand up to me?

16:37.204 --> 16:40.833
The guy
who stubbornly clings to BLACK DRAGON

16:41.417 --> 16:43.961
and the guy who was BLACK DRAGON's wallet.

16:43.961 --> 16:48.090
Has Izana satisfied you, Inui?

16:48.090 --> 16:51.844
Are you still
just Toman's wallet, Kokonoi?

16:51.844 --> 16:55.514
Know your place,
you worthless pieces of trash.

16:56.223 --> 16:58.267
Hanagaki, escape out the back.

16:58.267 --> 17:00.227
- Huh?
- Naoto Tachibana,

17:00.853 --> 17:03.272
expose the truth behind Hakkai's death.

17:04.356 --> 17:07.609
I don't know
how he managed to get so close to Sano,

17:07.609 --> 17:10.904
but I'm absolutely sure
Izana Kurokawa was behind it.

17:11.488 --> 17:13.615
Avenge my brother's death.

17:14.116 --> 17:15.617
- Got it?
- I will.

17:15.617 --> 17:16.744
Go!

17:16.744 --> 17:17.870
Takemichi.

17:18.454 --> 17:20.873
Taiju, thank you for everything.

17:22.166 --> 17:25.002
This settles my old debt to you.

17:26.003 --> 17:27.963
- Takemichi!
- Okay.

17:29.673 --> 17:32.551
- Get back here, scumbags!
- Hey, get back!

17:39.224 --> 17:43.145
I haven't had a good brawl in a long time.

17:46.899 --> 17:49.818
Better make this a fun one, Toman!

17:49.818 --> 17:53.197
- Tsk.
- Still a man stuck in the past.

17:58.619 --> 17:59.870
<i>Inupi and Koko.</i>

18:00.370 --> 18:03.373
<i>Could those two be the key
to learning about Izana Kurokawa?</i>

18:04.291 --> 18:05.709
Naoto!

18:05.709 --> 18:07.419
What's wrong, Takemichi?

18:07.419 --> 18:09.254
- We've got to go back.
- What?

18:09.254 --> 18:11.173
Those two must know.

18:11.673 --> 18:14.802
I want to know more
about the Kanto Incident.

18:14.802 --> 18:16.386
I'm going back.

18:16.386 --> 18:18.097
Takemichi...

18:19.681 --> 18:21.141
Takemitchy.

18:25.562 --> 18:26.605
Huh?

18:35.614 --> 18:36.615
Kisaki...

18:37.199 --> 18:38.700
Die.

18:51.130 --> 18:52.214
Naoto?

18:56.468 --> 18:58.887
Naoto!

18:58.887 --> 19:01.140
Tsk. Dumb move.

19:01.140 --> 19:03.142
Hang in there, Naoto!

19:03.809 --> 19:06.186
Takemichi... run.

19:09.314 --> 19:10.941
Hey, hey, now.

19:11.608 --> 19:15.320
Naoto Tachibana
was supposed to be mine to kill, Kisaki.

19:15.821 --> 19:17.531
Sorry, Izana.

19:17.531 --> 19:19.700
He took the bullet meant for Takemitchy.

19:19.700 --> 19:20.993
<i>Izana?</i>

19:26.415 --> 19:29.543
You guys killed my Mikey.

19:30.627 --> 19:32.045
<i>"My Mikey"?</i>

19:32.796 --> 19:33.922
Kakucho.

19:40.679 --> 19:41.680
Kaku-chan...

19:43.056 --> 19:44.141
Kill him.

19:44.641 --> 19:45.934
Yes, sir.

19:49.980 --> 19:51.356
Kaku-chan...

19:55.694 --> 19:58.822
I've devoted my life to him.

20:14.755 --> 20:16.924
<i>I've been shot. I've been shot!</i>

20:24.973 --> 20:25.974
Nice work.

20:28.936 --> 20:30.854
That ended all too fast.

20:33.649 --> 20:36.026
<i>Damn it! Damn it!</i>

20:37.778 --> 20:39.905
Naoto, I'm sorry...

20:40.572 --> 20:41.823
Takemichi...

20:42.783 --> 20:46.078
When I first found you as an adult,

20:46.870 --> 20:48.288
I fell into despair.

20:50.165 --> 20:51.917
I thought,

20:51.917 --> 20:56.463
"Do I really have to put all my trust
in this pathetic loser?"

20:57.839 --> 21:02.135
"What did my sister even see in this guy?"

21:02.135 --> 21:03.679
It was a mystery to me.

21:05.264 --> 21:09.142
But after seeing you fail
over and over again,

21:09.142 --> 21:11.603
this is what I think.

21:11.603 --> 21:15.524
This is what a real hero is.

21:17.317 --> 21:19.820
Despite all your failures,
you never give up.

21:21.530 --> 21:22.531
Takemichi,

21:23.031 --> 21:26.118
I am proud of you.

21:26.618 --> 21:28.578
Naoto...

21:30.455 --> 21:32.457
This will be our final handshake...

21:34.084 --> 21:35.168
Takemichi.

21:36.712 --> 21:40.173
Death really is frightening, isn't it?

21:42.551 --> 21:43.635
Now...

21:44.803 --> 21:46.596
before I breathe my last.

21:49.641 --> 21:51.810
<i>This won't be the last time, Naoto.</i>

21:59.860 --> 22:02.112
<i>I won't let it be the last.</i>

22:04.239 --> 22:06.074
<i>There's no way...</i>

22:07.284 --> 22:08.744
<i>I will ever give up!</i>

23:39.751 --> 23:41.753
Translated by Brian Athey
